<title>USA: Van Eck in deal with Shanghai firm.</title>
<headline>Van Eck in deal with Shanghai firm.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Van Eck Global said it signed a deal with Shanghai-based Shenyin &amp; Wanguo Securities to create a joint-venture management company to be based in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Van Eck said the venture was the first between a U.S.-based mutual fund company and Shenyin, which it called the largest securities firm in China.</p>
<p>The firm, to be 51 percent owned by Shenyin and 49 percent by Van Eck, will offer asset management services.</p>
<p>Shenyin has total assets of US$1.9 billion and 3,000 employees, according to Van Eck.</p>
<p>Van Eck Global has $1.8 billion in assets under management.</p>
